Open the site in burp, login as wiener/peter, check the requests. You will find a GET /user/lookup?user=wiener request in http history. Send this request to repeater.
Lets try to get an error message. Put a ' behind the username value:
{
  "message": "There was an error getting user details"
}
If we chane the url end to '+' we will get back our login credentials. Lets give the server to a false condition:' && '1'=='2
As response we will get: Could not find user. If you change the condition to a true one: '1'=='1 you will get back your credentials.
Notice, that if you change the username value to administrator, you will get back the administrators credentials. Now we have to find out the administrators password.
As first, lets find out the passwords length. Change the request url's end to: ' && this.password.length < 10 || 'a'=='b
This means, if the password is shorter then 10 chars, then its true, and give back the administrators credentials. if longer than 10, it will show us an error.
I found out that at 8 i got an error, and at 9 i still have the credentials, this means the password is 8 characters long.
To identify the passowrd we will use this payload:
' && this.password[0]=='a
This means that the first character from the password is 'a' if we get back the credentials, then its true (we have a match), if its false we will get an error.
